-- title:
--   Half-unit g=cₓ v at a crossing node, Igusa-separated
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$; write $A_0=A\cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, Henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Give $\overline{\mathbb Q}$'s modular function field $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (level $q^2M'$ with $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$) the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the structure map. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of that extension over $k_0$, every valuation subring $W_0\subseteq F_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$, discretely valued with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$; every local Noetherian subring $O\subseteq W_0$ of $F_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$, such that every element of $O$ is congruent modulo nonunits to some element of $k_0\cap A$ lying in $O$, and with $F_0$ the field of fractions of $O$; every $E_0\ge 1$ with $\pi_0\in O$, all $c_x,c_y\in O$, $u\in O^\times$, every ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto the $UV$-crossing model $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, satisfying $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, compatibility of $\iota$ with constants from $k_0\cap A$, $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V V$; every valuation subring $W_x\supseteq O$ of $F_0$ that is discretely valued with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal; and every local subring $O'$ of $F_0$ and subring $B_c\subseteq O\cap O'$ such that both $O$ and $O'$ consist exactly of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit wherever it lies in the respective ring: if some $f\in O'$ lies outside $W_x$, then there exists $g\in O\cap O'$ with $g=c_x v$ for some unit $v$ of $O$ and with $g$ a unit of $O'$.
--
--   This is the two-node half-unit step in the analysis of a crossing-presented node on the full-level modular curve: starting from the $UV$-crossing presentation of the completed local ring and from the separation of the second branch ring $O'$ from the valuation ring $W_x$ of the first branch, it produces an element of the common chart that is simultaneously $c_x$ times a unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$. It is used in the construction of layered node presentations at nodes of the Igusa-type reduction, and it relies on the power identity $h^{E_0+1}=c_x\cdot(\text{nonunit})$ supplied by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_pow_eq_mul_nonunit_of_mem_maximalIdeal_igusaBranch_of_node_crossingPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_pow_eq_mul_nonunit_of_mem_maximalIdeal_igusaBranch_of_node_crossingPresentation).
